    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Prayer for Restoration"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "For the choir director. A psalm of David, when the prophet Nathan came to him after he had gone to Bathsheba."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Be gracious to me, God,",
          "according to your faithful love;",
          "according to your abundant compassion,",
          "blot out my rebellion."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Completely wash away my guilt",
          "and cleanse me from my sin."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For I am conscious of my rebellion,",
          "and my sin is always before me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Against you #— #you alone #— #I have sinned",
          "and done this evil in your sight.",
          "So you are right when you pass sentence;",
          "you are blameless when you judge."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Indeed, I was guilty when I was born;",
          "I was sinful when my mother conceived me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely you desire integrity in the inner self,",
          "and you teach me wisdom deep within."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Purify me with hyssop, and I will be clean;",
          "wash me, and I will be whiter than snow."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let me hear joy and gladness;",
          "let the bones you have crushed rejoice."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Turn your face away from my sins",
          "and blot out all my guilt."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God, create a clean heart for me",
          "and renew a steadfast spirit within me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do not banish me from your presence",
          "or take your Holy Spirit from me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Restore the joy of your salvation to me,",
          "and sustain me by giving me a willing spirit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then I will teach the rebellious your ways,",
          "and sinners will return to you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Save me from the guilt of bloodshed, God —",
          "God of my salvation —",
          "and my tongue will sing of your righteousness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lord, open my lips,",
          "and my mouth will declare your praise."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You do not want a sacrifice, or I would give it;",
          "you are not pleased with a burnt offering."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The sacrifice pleasing to God is a broken spirit.",
          "You will not despise a broken and humbled heart, God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In your good pleasure, cause Zion to prosper;",
          "build the walls of Jerusalem."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then you will delight in righteous sacrifices,",
          "whole burnt offerings;",
          "then bulls will be offered on your altar."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
